    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49c579d9_b59cde0f",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_flash/cros_flash_em32f967_wp.h",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1177449
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T02:51:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are not checking protection by testing write behavior.\nOur implementation reads the hardware Protect Area configuration registers and determines protection based on the configured start address, size, and enable bit.\nFor reference, this is the register format we use:\n```\ntypedef union\n{\n    struct\n    {\n      __IO uint32_t STARTADDR : 20;\n      __IO uint32_t Reserved  : 4;\n      __IO uint32_t PAGES     : 7;\n      __IO uint32_t ENABLEN   : 1;\n    }Protect_S;\n        __IO uint32_t Protect;\n}Protect_U_t;\n```\nSo the logic is based on configured protection state, similar in spirit to how the reference driver checks SRP/WPS bits—but in our case the protection mechanism is implemented inside the MCU through these Protect Area registers. Does this make sense to you?",
      "parentUuid": "fd3a0560_6fbf5f22",
      "revId": "c768fb84b0673458119d52d90e855e2d801ac088",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
